{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/420644-can-you-make-a-pact-for-a-relationship-to-another-demon","id":420644,"title":"Can you make a pact for a relationship to another demon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-26T14:17:52-08:00","id":420644,"title":"Can you make a pact for a relationship to another demon?","content":"It occured to me while trying out Demon last weekend that it might happen that a Demon tries to make a pact with a human to get a relationship, but that this relationship would be another demon.<br /> <br /> From what I could understand of the rules, a demon can sign a contract with a human to get one of their relationships trasferred to them. Like a friend or wife or chesspartner or whatever. The friend in question would have his memories altered to believe that the demon had always been friend instead of the human that signs the contract.<br /> <br /> But what happens in the following scenario:<br /> <br /> Demon A wants to sign a pact with Human B to get Friend C. However, unbeknownst of both A and B, Friend C is actually a Cover of Demon C.<br /> <br /> Does the pact work as normal, or does it fail? And if it fails, is it impossible to sign, or does Demon C retain their memories, or will C not be transferred even though B signed the pact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:21:15-08:00","id":420719,"title":"","content":"I would say that no change happens to C. Like I might rule that C is aware that something shifted and there was something that happened to the cover if they were in it, but since a demon doesn't have the memories or knowledge of a cover then C would only be aware of the specifics if they encountered the altered situations. For example lets say the alteration to C's cover altered photos so that instead of the old picture of C &amp; B hanging out at some hiking trail or what have you it now shows C &amp;A instead. C would recall that the photos used to show B instead of A and would know something is up, but would not know the specifics that couldn't be gleamed through the visible images.<br /> <br /> The contract would succeed in that Cover C would now have been/be A's friend, however the demon is an abstract observer and would not be altered or accommodated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:28:47-08:00","id":420724,"title":"","content":"At a guess, I'd say C's memories remain unaltered, but if B was a part of C's Cover, than C may have to make a Compromise roll. With regard to the pact, it'd likely fail, since the 'transfer' couldn't work. A would obviously be aware of this, and probably suspect B to be some kind of G-M agent or plant, and go into hiding and never, ever, <i>ever</i> contact anyone even remotely connected to B.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:55:04-08:00","id":420760,"title":"","content":"I'd say C's memories would not change, but he would know something happened. Allan53 is spot on.<br /> <br /> As for Compromise...depends? I'd say yes if C got the friendship via a Pact, and no if it was organic, but I might say no in general. It depends.<br /> <br /> As Allan53 says though, it would probably spook (maybe Spook) C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:08:04-08:00","id":420768,"title":"","content":"I was mostly thinking if B was a part of C's cover would the Compromise roll be necessary. But also, since Pacts work through the infrastructure of the G-M, albeit in a weird way, a failed one may send up a ping, which may or may not be noticed or acted on. But since Demons have a very strong vested interest in being as insanely paranoid as possible, definitely would make both A and C skittish, at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}